The Catch: Avoid the Generalist Trap
If you try to launch a product simply named "Soft Life Course" or "Soft Life Planner", you risk getting buried in social media noise. The keyword is highly saturated as a generic hashtag. 
To turn this into a true money-maker, you must sub-niche and combine it with a functional utility. Instead of selling the abstract concept of a soft life, sell the exact tool or system that builds it. For example:
Generic: How to live a Soft Life. (Low conversion)
High-Converting Money Hook: The Soft Life System: How to Automate Your Solopreneur Business to Work 15 Hours a Week.
